# Generated data files, left in the shape their generator writes.
#
# These are produced by scripts/manifest/*.js and scripts/blog/*.js with
# JSON.stringify at two spaces, and they are committed from CI, where the
# pre-commit hook does not run. So prettier has never formatted them, and the
# committed shape is the generator's shape.
#
# Formatting them locally would put the committed file permanently at odds with
# its generator: prettier collapses short arrays onto one line, the generator
# expands them again, and seo-auto-update.yml regenerates after every merge and
# commits whatever differs. That is a second full production build of every
# Vercel project, forever, for a whitespace disagreement. Verified before adding
# this: `prettier --check` reports all six manifests in this change as needing
# edits, while `git show HEAD:<file>` is the generator's formatting.
#
# Hand-edited data is deliberately not listed. captions.json files, date
# overrides and tags.json are written by people and should be formatted.

src/images/Portfolios/**/*-manifest.json
sites/mcc-cal-vite/public-vite/manifests/
sites/mcc-cal-vite/api/manifests/data/

src/content/blog/blog-manifest.json
src/content/blog/feed.json
src/content/blog/feed.xml
